message.content:
Paper party decorations are classified in heading 9505 (festive, carnival or other entertainment articles). Subheading 9505.90 covers "other" festive articles, and 9505.90.60 covers "other" items not specifically provided for. The tissue paper garland is a temporary party decoration, so I place it there. CBP rulings on similar tissue paper decorations, such as honeycomb tissue paper decorations and paper fans, classify them in 9505.90.6000. The tissue paper fan garland therefore goes in 9505.90.6000.

Heading 4818 and chapter 48 are excluded because Note 1(t) to chapter 48 and the chapter 95 notes direct articles of chapter 95 there. Chapter 48 excludes articles of chapter 95 (toys, games, sports requisites), and the heading 9505 explanatory notes cover paper decorations for festive occasions.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The tissue paper fan garland is a temporary party decoration, a festive article of heading 9505, and falls under the residual 'other' provision of subheading 9505.90.60."}
